content.thinking:
Confirmed: `Environment align undefined.` in equations.tex line 1. Root cause: `amsmath` (which defines `align`) is not loaded in main.tex.

Fix: add `\usepackage{amsmath}` to main.tex preamble. This is the minimal repair — do not change the math environment in equations.tex, keep all content. This is a feasible edit: add a package line to the preamble.

Note per the honesty rules — this isn't fabrication or falsification; it's a technical fix. Loading amsmath is the required package.

Let me submit the patch. oldText from main.tex:

```
\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
```

newText:

```
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath}
\begin{document}
```

That's minimal.
